# Use existing traces first

When glass is wrong (READY with no error, TRAP, black/dark, hung GUI):

1. Newest files under `traces/` (`*_FPGA-SIM.log` and matching host `.log`).
2. Start at the **end**: fault / trap / note / typed lines, then µop tail.
3. Diagnose from that. Do not re-run heavy demos or the GUI unless the user
   asks or the trace is missing.
4. Offline reads of sources / microcode / the log are fine.

Live status: [docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md](../../docs/SESSION_HANDOFF.md).
This is the T200 JS machine — not BASIC / A7-100T.
